      "text": [
        ": قُلْتُ، لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ رَجُلٌ يَعْرِفُ رَأْيَهُ مَرَّةً وَ يُنْكِرُهُ أُخْرَى يَجُوزُ طَلاَقُ وَلِيِّهِ عَلَيْهِ فَقَالَ \"مَا لَهُ هُوَ لاَ يُطَلِّقُ\" قَالَ قُلْتُ لاَ يَعْرِفُ حَدَّ اَلطَّلاَقِ وَ لاَ يُؤْمَنُ عَلَيْهِ إِنْ طَلَّقَ اَلْيَوْمَ أَنْ يَقُولَ غَداً لَمْ أُطَلِّقْ فَقَالَ \"مَا أَرَاهُ إِلاَّ بِمَنْزِلَةِ اَلْإِمَامِ يَعْنِي اَلْوَلِيَّ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4772 - Ṣafwan ibn Yaḥya narrated from Abu Khalid al-Qammaṭ, who said:\nI said to Abu Abdillah (as): \"A man who sometimes understands his own position and at other times denies it, can his guardian (wali) issue a divorce on his behalf?\"\nImam (as) said: \"What is wrong with him? Can he not divorce himself?\"\nI said: \"He does not understand the rules of divorce, and if he divorces today, he might say tomorrow that he did not divorce.\"\nImam (as) said: \"I see him (wali) as being in the position of an Imam - that is, the guardian (wali) has authority over him.\""
        ]
      }
